<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jalairs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jalayir tribe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Jalairs were a Mongol tribe that served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a> and his successors; his general Muqali was a Jalair. Jalair commanders were prominent in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, and after its collapse one of them, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-buzurg">Hasan Buzurg</a>, founded the Jalayirid dynasty in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> in the 1330s. Other Jalair groups became part of the Chagatai realm and of the Kazakh Senior Zhuz.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jalairs.jpg" alt="Jalairs" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Khiruge · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Homeland_of_the_Jalair_tribe_of_the_Mongol_Empire_in_1207.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…khans and the practical power of the great tribal groupings — among them the Dughlat in the east and the Barlas, <b>Jalayir</b> and Qara'una in the west — whose military strength made them the khanate's effective rulers whenever a khan lacked the personal authority to enforce his will.</blockquote><a href="/empire/chagatai-empire">Chagatai Empire · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Jalayirs</b> were a Mongol tribe prominent in the Ilkhanate.</blockquote><a href="/state/jalayirids">Jalayirids</a></li><li><blockquote>Its tribes, such as the Dulat, Uysun and <b>Jalayir</b>, were nomadic herders closely tied to the oasis cities of Tashkent and Turkistan.</blockquote><a href="/state/senior-juz">Senior Juz</a></li><li><blockquote>Real power lay with the Turkic and Mongol tribal amirs of the Barlas, <b>Jalayir</b>, Arlat and Qara'unas, who had settled among the towns of Transoxiana and adopted Islam.</blockquote><a href="/state/western-chagatai-khanate">Western Chagatai Khanate</a></li></ul></section>
